{{!-- Size, as a pill.

      Size is the one rating that is a CATEGORY rather than a quantity — a hamlet is not more than a
      village the way Defenses +2 is more than +1. Given the ratings' idiom (a value written on a
      rule, with a label beside it) it read as a sixth number in a row of numbers, and the band it
      carries ("2500+") read as that number's note.

      So it gets its own shape: one chip, no label, no rule, the tier and its population band on one
      line — "Stonetop, a city of 2500+". A category and a quantity share neither a control idiom nor
      a table row.

      Still a real select element, with the native chrome removed and the blank "unset" option the
      snapshot supplies preserved: an unchosen Size must not silently read as "hamlet".

      Params: attrData (the Size RatingSnapshot). --}}
<span class="steading-size-pill{{#unless attrData.current}} is-unset{{/unless}}">
	<select class="steading-attr-input steading-size-select"
	        data-change-action="attribute" data-attr="size"
	        aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.a11y.ratingValue' rating=attrData.title}}"
	        {{#unless @root.editable}}disabled{{/unless}}>
		{{#each attrData.options}}
			<option value="{{value}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{label}}</option>
		{{/each}}
	</select>
	{{#if (hasText attrData.note)}}<span class="steading-size-band">{{attrData.note}}</span>{{/if}}
</span>
